{"id":"KH0087","aliases":["AS074"],"contributors":"Marcia & Robert Ascher","kfgUrl":"https://www.khipufieldguide.com/catalog/KH0087.html","museum":{"name":"Musee Quai Branly (previous names: Musee de l Homme, Mus\u00e9e d'Ethnographie du Trocad\u00e9ro)","canonical":"Mus\u00e9e du quai Branly","number":"71.1964.19.1.7","city":"Paris","country":"France","url":"https://collections.quaibranly.fr/","description":null},"provenance":"Nazca Valley; Ancon, Central Coast","region":null,"created":"02/10/1970","primary":{"structure":"P","thick":0.0,"length":56.5,"color":"YB","colorParsed":[{"codes":["YB"]}],"fiber":"CN","beginning":"T","term":"K","twist":"S","notes":"1.A detached pendant was associated with the quipu. It is color MB, has length 22.o cm with a finished end, and has value 0 (or blank). We assume it comes from position 67.<br/>2. Quipus AS74-As80 are contained in a wicker basket. The Museum designates this as given by Henry Reichlen and from the Nazca Valley. Further, AS74-AS79 are noted as from Inca burials, Ancon, Central Coast. The basket has a hinged lid and is rectangular in shape (40 cm. x 18 cm. x 11 cm). Also contained in the basket are 2 black (LK) wool cords of 408 cm. and 224 cm.; 27 prepared pendant blanks (12W and 15B) all 28.o cm..-31.ocm. in length, strung on a loop of cord (color B); 7 smooth pebbles; and 79 beans. The beans have been identified by Professor Lawrence Kaplan, University of Massachusettes as seeds of Phaseolus vulgaris, the common bean.<br/>By spacing, AS74 contains 1 group of 5 pendants; 2 single pendants; 9 groups of 5 pendants each; a single short differently colored cord serving as a marker; and 8 groups of 5 pendants each.<br/>4. With the exception of 1 pendant (P1), all groups of 5 pendants have the same color pattern: YB, W, W MB, B. Subsidiaries appear only on the second pendant in the groups and all are colored MB-W.<br/>5. By spacing, marker, and values, the quipu is in 3 parts: part I is 7 pendants (1 group if 5 and 3 singles); part II is 9 groups; and part III is 8 groups. All pendants in the part II are zero valued (or blank); all in part III have values 0-10; and part I has larger values and 2 values on some pendants. On 2 of the double-valued pendants, the lower value equals the sum of the values in the corresponding pendant position in the groups of part III.<br/>6. We hypothesize that part I in some way serves as a summary of the other 2 parts and that the 9 blank groups indicate that the quipu is incomplete.<br/>7. Comparison of AS74-AS80:"},"groups":[{"start":2.5,"first":1,"last":5,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":4.0,"first":6,"last":6,"n":1,"spacing":0.0},{"start":5.0,"first":7,"last":7,"n":1,"spacing":0.0},{"start":6.5,"first":8,"last":12,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":8.0,"first":13,"last":17,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":9.5,"first":18,"last":22,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":11.0,"first":23,"last":27,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":12.5,"first":28,"last":32,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":14.0,"first":33,"last":37,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":15.5,"first":38,"last":42,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":17.0,"first":43,"last":47,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":18.5,"first":48,"last":52,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":20.0,"first":53,"last":53,"n":1,"spacing":0.0},{"start":20.5,"first":54,"last":58,"n":5,"spacing":0.167},{"start":21.5,"first":59,"last":63,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":23.0,"first":64,"last":68,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":24.5,"first":69,"last":73,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":26.0,"first":74,"last":78,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":27.5,"first":79,"last":83,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":29.0,"first":84,"last":88,"n":5,"spacing":0.5},{"start":30.5,"first":89,"last":93,"n":5,"spacing":25.0}],"cords":[{"name":"p1","level":1,"kind":"pendant","twist":"S","attach":"R","length":29.0,"term":"K","thick":null,"color":"W","value":122,"altValue":0,"knots":[{"n":1,"type":"S","pos":7.0,"dir":"S","value":100},{"n":2,"type":"S","pos":8.5,"dir":"S","value":20},{"n":2,"type":"L","pos":15